/-!
# Original critical-orbit noncentrality before plane equality

The second fixed layer of the entire moved cover lies in the maximal
critical plane. Hence a subgroup of Q-alpha centralizing that plane sends
the opposite Z-layer into the plane. Apply the normal-closure argument
with N generated by Z-c intersect Q-alpha. This proves that the orbit has
nontrivial residual action modulo Z-alpha and that its generating plane
escapes the literal fixed-space preimage.

Neither plane equality, an elementary radical image, a Sylow assumption
nor a favorable-pair estimate is used. The remaining favorable-pair
calculation and distance-two exhaustion assembly are still required.
Source: MS93 (3.6), printed p.871, before the favorable orientation.
-/

public noncomputable section
